On Wed, 2 Sep 1998 rej at DMU.dk wrote:

> This question might be naive. Is it possible to think of a LOESS-model
> with a binomial response variable? And if so, can it be done in S-Plus?

Yes, no (except in simple cases by gam and lo), but take a look at Clive
Loader's locfit library at

http://cm.bell-labs.com/stat/project/locfit

and in the one-regressor case also sm.logit in the Bowman-Azzalini library
sm (on statlib I believe).

More details and examples in the on-line statistics complements to V&R.

