From belliney at idt.net  Sun Sep  6 23:11:49 1998
From: belliney at idt.net (Eran Bellin, M.D.)
Date: Sun, 06 Sep 1998 19:11:49 -0400
Subject: [S] survival vs survival symptom free analysis
Message-ID: <35F316B5.4897DAD9@idt.net>

September 6, 1998

To members of this list:

Attached is a dataframe called data3.  It was created with the data.dump
command.

In it are the variables

> names(data3)
[1] "group"  "censor" "Time"

with which you can create a Kaplan Meier survival statistic using
plot(surv.fit) command.

There are two groups.

Group 1 is a group of cancer patients surviving.  Censorship occurs when
censor=0 and means that the patient has been lost to follow up..
Group 2 is the same group of cancer patients surviving without
symptoms.  The endpoint is symptom and death is considered a censoring
event.

I am able to perform simple Kaplan-Meier plots using the commands:

> plot(surv.fit(data3$Time,data3$censor,data3$group))

I would like to do the following:

  i. Draw hatched patterns between the KM plot of group1 and group2
  ii. Calculate the area between group1 and group2 with the option of
only evaluating this area between time zero and any time I choose on the
graph (example time=60).

In addition, I would like to take advantage of the confidence intervals
that can be generated about a KM plot and plotthe lower limit confidence
interval of group1 and the upper limit confidence interval (95%) of
group2.  With this new plot, I would like to repeat i and ii above.
(Drawing a hatched pattern and then calculating the area).

In addition, I would like to take advantage of the confidence intervals
that can be generated about a Km plot and plot the upper limit
confidence interval of group 1 and the lower limit confidence interval
of group2.  With this new plot, I would like to repeat i and ii above.

Thanks for your advice.

Sincerely,

Eran Bellin
