Subject: [S] Catastrophe curves
Message-ID: <199809080419.QAA29849@grunt.marc.cri.nz>

For calculating contour lines to fit binomial data, glms often work
well.  However, there are times when they are still too linear to
represent a response surface that has sudden changes.

For this reason, I was interested to hear from anyone who has had
experience fitting catastrophe curves to percentage data.

I shall, of course, make a summary for the list.

Thanks.

Patrick
