I think the easiest way would be to convert the factor column to a
character vector, then you can change in the way you have done before.
Then you can turn it back into a factor which will recognise the new level.

I usually find most objects are easier to manipulate if they aren't
factors because you often don't know if it's using the level or the
code.  It's simple enough to return it to a factor when you're
finished.  I've been fooled many times before but not since I adopted
this approach.

Cheers

Patrick

