1. Check the class of your variable using class(x) - seems as if it might
have been converted to factor. If it is factor, use as.character(x) to
convert to character,then use dates(x) to convert to date class. Given the
importance of these types of changes, I prefer to do them in two stages and
check after each stage. First finding the NAs - not always a trivial task.
Then converting the NAs.

2. For the alive patients, you should use the date last known to be alive
rather than the ending date of the study. It is always risky to presume
patients are alive without documented evidence like a phone call or office
visit.

