From mcw at ln.nimh.nih.gov  Fri Sep 18 16:45:08 1998
From: mcw at ln.nimh.nih.gov (Matthew Wiener)
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 1998 12:45:08 -0400
Subject: [S] multiple symbols in a single graph -- solution
Message-ID: <Pine.SGI.3.96.980918124224.27830C-100000@ln.nimh.nih.gov>

Two ways to put multiple symbols:

1.  "old" graphics

plot(x, y, type = "n")  # axes only 
text(x, y, sym[g])  # does the plot (where g is a variable defining the
                                     groups, possibly a factor)

2.  Trellis graphs

use panel.superpose:

xyplot(Life.Exp~Murder, panel=panel.superpose, groups=Region,data=d,
        pch=c("N","S","M","W")) 

Thanks to Bill Venables and Bill Dunlap.

Matt Wiener

