Subject: [S] competing risks and cumulative conditional probability of cause-specific failure
Message-ID: <98Sep21.130045edt.115610@gateway.healthlink.on.ca>

The issue of competing risks is a real concern when considering
cause-specific failure, particularly in cancers such as breast and prostate.
Kaplan-Meier curves are not appropriate for summarizing failure time data
such as local recurrence since K-M curves over-estimate the probability of
cause-specific failure when there is a high mortality rate. Pepe and Mori
[Statistics in Medicine, Vol.12, 737-751 (1993)] propose the use of
cumulative incidence and cumulative conditional probability to accurately
give the probability and risk of cause-specific failure.

Has anyone seen or developed algorithms in Splus to address this issue?
Any help would be greatly appreciated.

Thanks in advance.

